The '''districts of Lacashe''' are the first-level administrative divisions of the [[Lacashe|Republic of Lacashe]]. The country is divided into thirteen districts and the [[Guledga Capital District]], a separate administrative unit of the same status that contains the capital, [[Guledga]]. Each district is subdivided into municipalities and communes. {{As of|2026}} the fourteen units together hold a population of 9,853,423 over an area of 221,704 square kilometres.

Six districts along the southwestern coast and in the southern interior bear names in the [[Burawi language]], given during the settlement of the colonial [[Province of Lacashe]]. The remaining eight, covering the northern and eastern interior, bear names derived from the {{W|Tapuya language}} and written in Burawi orthography; they preserve the toponymy of the [[Tapuya Confederacy]] country that preceded the colony.

